I believe the reason that you can't set defaults from settings page or via API is because the same values will be assigned to several different items by different authors. For example; for items with same url, the same settings will be shared on them and applied to each item, thus overriding some values you would like to customize. Therefore, you have to specify whether to delete existing default settings when saving a new one so they will not replace those already present.
For items without url, it all depends of other settings if the authors want to share certain values across items, else just creating them separately for each item.
@Mike_Hobbs Thank you! I wasn't aware of that. Regarding deleted defaults, are there any plans to implement them as well? That'd be incredibly helpful!
There is an option on each settings page to "replace existing defaults", so it's safe to change defaults in bulk (though, after editing them to make sure they're correct;
